so you've finished Pokemon Scarlet or  Violet and you're wondering what to do  next well we've got you covered even  without the battle tower here are some  activities that will keep you busy for  dozens of hours technically scarlet and  Violet's story doesn't end with the  credits geta will ask you to check in on  all the gym leaders in paldea of course  a check-in means a battle and each gym  leader will hit you with everything  they've got once you've defeated all the  gym leaders for a second time you will  be able to participate in the school  tournament this allows you to rematch  your friends and teachers at top form  you'll need to do it at least once to  complete the post game story content but  you can technically participate in the  tournament as many times as you want  Additionally you can also battle team  star generals again if you return to  their bases once you've completed the  tournament Jacques will give you a call  and tell you about difficult Terror  raids popping up all over paldea do a  few of these and he'll call you again to  warn you about even tougher 6 star raids  six star raids have a pink glowing  outline on the map and can be  significantly tougher than 5 Star rates  depending on the Pokemon and its typing  when it comes to these raids I highly  recommend squatting up with some friends  or matchmaking with randoms you can  always join raids as well via the Poke  portal in the pause menu but it can be  tough actually getting into raids from  this menu your best bet is to wait until  you can refresh the raid list and join  something quickly so why should you do  all these difficult raids the rewards  for completing five and six star raids  are usually worth the trouble 5 and 6  star rates typically feature rare  Pokemon with fantastic bass stats even  if you do manage to catch one of these  rare Pokemon in the wild its stats will  be inferior you can check a Pokemon's  base stats or individual values by  pressing Plus on a Pokemon in the boxes  menu the word best next to a specific  stat means it's IV for that stat is  perfect no good means it's IV for that  stat is zero it's worth noting that you  can't see a Pokemon's IVs until you  finish the game and stopped by a Pokemon  Center doing so will unlock the judge  function along with powerful Pokemon 5  and 6 star rates could potentially net  you some rare items ability capsules  ability patches and urban mystica  ability capsules let you change a  Pokemon's ability while ability patches  let you change a Pokemon's ability to  its hidden ability if it has one these  items are incredibly useful if you plan  on putting together some competitive  teams meanwhile Urban mystica if used  properly can dramatically increase your  odds of finding a shiny Pokemon if  you're having trouble with these raids I  recommend heading back to the depths of  area 0 to catch your extramaridon or  Corydon depending on which version you  own you can technically use your ride  legendarian raids but it's nice having  an extra one in your boxes just in case  along with meridon and Corydon there are  four other legendary Pokemon you can  catch in order to crack one of these bad  boys open you need to pull eight  matching Stakes out of the ground once  you've found all eight the volt will  crumble and you can battle and catch the  legendary Pokemon if you're having  trouble finding these vaults then maybe  it's time to finish your education there  are a ton of classes you can take at the  Mesa goza Academy and completing them  will earn you some nice rewards if you  complete the history course for example  the professor will Mark all four volts  on your map of course you'll still need  to find all the corresponding Stakes to  unlock that Vault participating in  Terror rates and hunting down  legendaries will also fill out your  Pokedex if you're into shiny hunting I'd  make this a priority if you complete  your Pokedex Jacques will give you the  shiny charm which doubles your odds of  running into a shiny if shiny hunting  isn't quite your thing then maybe put  this one on the back burner if you're  looking for some more shiny hunting tips  though check out my other video on the  subject I'll drop a link in the end if  competitive battling is your thing  another satisfying time sync is Pokemon  breeding most pokemon you catch in the  wild will have poor stats the best way  to get a specific Pokemon with great  stats is through Pokemon breeding find  and catch two compatible Pokemon put  them both in your party set up a picnic  and make an egg power sandwich over time  time the basket will fill up with  Pokemon eggs typically a newly hatched  Pokemon will get a random nature and it  will randomly inherit three IVs from the  parents the goal is to hatch better and  better Pokemon which can eventually be  subbed in for the parents to produce  even better Pokemon there are a few  items that make this process easier  though a destiny knot allows the parents  to pass down 5 random IVs instead of  three from the parents and an Everstone  means The Offspring will have the same  nature honestly breeding deserves an  entire video on its own there's a lot to  it but if this is a path you're  interested in going down I highly  recommend checking out our Pokemon  breeding guide it was written with sword  and shield in mind but some of the more  in-depth concepts are still true in  scarlet and violet in the meantime I  highly recommend hunting down a five or  six star ditto raid that should net you  a near perfect ditto that you can use to  breed almost anything the story is only  the tip of the iceberg when it comes to  Pokemon games hopefully this video will  help you get the most out of your post  game Adventure in Pokemon scarlet and  violet and if you're interested in the  competitive scene I highly recommend  checking out our competitive Pokemon  explained video series on Gamespot thank  you so much for watching  [Music]
 

